---
term: Charter lifecycle
section: charter-lifecycle
order: 10
definition: The principle that a charter must be hard to amend in ways that would destroy the conditions for future legitimate amendment.
seeAlso:
  - anti-capture-protection
  - fundamental-protections
  - living-charter
---
This principle explains why [[tiered constitutional design]] makes fundamental protections the hardest provisions to change. It protects the constitutional process itself and leaves substantive policy free to change.

> The constitutional system should be difficult to amend in ways that destroy the conditions for future legitimate democratic amendment.
